    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are proud to present 72 St Anne's, Kimmage, Dublin 12 to the market, a superb home presented in turnkey condition throughout. Offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation over three levels, the property further benefits from a southerly facing rear garden and off-street parking for two cars, making it an ideal choice for those seeking a ready-to-occupy home in this popular and mature residential location.\n\nThe accommodation is both spacious and practical. At ground-floor level, a welcoming entrance hall leads through to a generous living room measuring approximately 4.18m x 3.69m, providing an inviting space for everyday family living. To the rear is a well-appointed kitchen measuring approximately 3.55m x 3.69m, with direct access to the rear garden. Useful storage and the staircase to the upper floors complete the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nOn the first floor there are two well-proportioned bedrooms, measuring approximately 3.69m x 2.66m and 3.69m x 1.87m respectively. A family bathroom and landing complete this level. The accommodation continues to the second floor where a generous attic room, measuring approximately 4.09m x 3.69m, provides excellent additional and versatile space suitable for a variety of uses.\n\nOutside, the southerly facing rear garden is a particularly attractive feature, enjoying excellent natural light and providing an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. To the front, the property benefits from off-street parking for two cars.\n\nNo. 72 offers an excellent combination of turnkey presentation, versatile accommodation and valuable outdoor space. Its well-designed layout and sought-after Kimmage setting are sure to appeal to first-time buyers, growing families and those looking to trade within the area.\n\nSt Anne's enjoys a highly convenient location in the heart of Kimmage, Dublin 12, a mature and well-established residential area popular with families and first-time buyers alike.\n\nThe property is within easy reach of an excellent selection of local shops, cafés and everyday amenities, while the neighbouring villages of Terenure, Harold's Cross and Rathgar are all readily accessible and offer a further variety of restaurants, cafés and shopping facilities.\n\nThe area is particularly well served by a number of highly regarded primary and secondary schools, together with an excellent choice of sporting and recreational amenities. Eamonn Ceannt Park, Bushy Park and a variety of local sports clubs are all within easy reach.\n\nTransport links are excellent, with numerous Dublin Bus services providing convenient access to the city centre and surrounding areas. The location also offers easy access to the N81, M50 and wider road network, making St Anne's an exceptionally convenient base within south Dublin."
      },
